---
// 1.3: a labelled sketch of the Power BI Desktop window (not a screenshot, so it never goes out of date as fast).
---
<figure class="cs-fig pbi">
  <span class="cs-figtag">Find your way around</span>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 680 360" role="img" aria-label="Sketch of the Power BI Desktop window: ribbon at the top, view buttons on the left, report canvas in the middle, Filters, Visualizations and Data panes on the right, page tabs at the bottom.">
    <rect class="box" x="4" y="4" width="672" height="340" rx="8" />
    <rect class="acc" x="4" y="4" width="672" height="46" rx="8" /><text class="b" x="16" y="24">1 Ribbon</text><text class="mu" x="16" y="41">Get data, Transform data (opens Power Query), New measure, Publish</text>
    <rect class="box" x="4" y="50" width="38" height="268" /><text class="b" x="10" y="78">2</text>
    <rect class="acc" x="12" y="88" width="22" height="20" rx="4" /><rect class="box" x="12" y="114" width="22" height="20" rx="4" /><rect class="box" x="12" y="140" width="22" height="20" rx="4" /><rect class="box" x="12" y="166" width="22" height="20" rx="4" /><rect class="box" x="12" y="192" width="22" height="20" rx="4" />
    <text class="mu" x="50" y="300">2 Views: Report, Table, Model, DAX query, TMDL</text>
    <rect class="box" x="58" y="62" width="380" height="226" rx="4" /><text class="b" x="70" y="84">3 Report canvas</text><text class="mu" x="70" y="102">drag fields here to build visuals</text>
    <rect class="acc" x="80" y="120" width="150" height="70" rx="4" /><text class="mu" x="90" y="160">a visual</text>
    <rect class="acc" x="250" y="120" width="170" height="150" rx="4" /><text class="mu" x="262" y="200">another visual</text>
    <rect class="box" x="448" y="50" width="70" height="268" /><text class="b" x="456" y="72">4</text><text class="mu" x="456" y="90">Filters</text>
    <rect class="box" x="518" y="50" width="78" height="268" /><text class="b" x="526" y="72">5</text><text class="mu" x="526" y="90">Visual-</text><text class="mu" x="526" y="106">izations</text><text class="mu" x="526" y="130">Build,</text><text class="mu" x="526" y="146">Format</text>
    <rect class="box" x="596" y="50" width="80" height="268" /><text class="b" x="604" y="72">6 Data</text><text class="mu" x="604" y="92">▸ Date</text><text class="mu" x="604" y="110">▸ Product</text><text class="mu" x="604" y="128">▸ Sales</text><text class="mu" x="604" y="146">▸ Store</text><text class="mu" x="604" y="164">▸ Targets</text>
    <rect class="box" x="4" y="318" width="672" height="26" /><text class="b" x="14" y="336">7 Page tabs</text><text class="mu" x="110" y="336">Page 1 · Page 2 · +</text>
    <text class="wm" x="670" y="356" text-anchor="end">fibub.com</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>1 The ribbon. 2 The views down the left side. 3 The canvas, where visuals live. 4 Filters for this visual, page or whole report. 5 Visualizations: pick a chart, then drop fields into its wells (Build) and style it (Format). 6 Data: your tables, columns and measures. 7 Pages. Microsoft moves buttons now and then; the names stay much the same.</figcaption>
</figure>
